  "_sourceRefs": [
    "Stedi (stedi.com/edi/hipaa/transaction-set/277-A1) — the HIPAA-specific (005010X212) 277 Health Care Claim Status Response transaction set, EDI Phase 6. GS01='HN'/GS08='005010X212' confirmed directly on this page. ST01='277' confirmed.",
    "PyX12's own free map repo (azoner/pyx12/pyx12/map) DOES ship a genuine 5010 map for this transaction — 277.5010.X212.xml (201KB) — the authoritative primary source used to cross-check HL03 codes and loop structure, matching this project's own established preference for PyX12 over Stedi's HTML summaries when both are available.",
    "Same 5-level HL hierarchy as 276.json (2000A/B/C/D/E, HL03=20/21/19/22/23 respectively — cross-checked directly against PyX12's raw XML, resolving an inconsistent Stedi HTML-page answer), but with two real, deliberate structural differences from 276: (1) 277 adds its own trace+status loops at the Information-Receiver and Service-Provider levels (2200B, 2200C — TRN+STC, 0/1 each) that 276 has no equivalent of, since only the RESPONSE reports status at every level the request could have asked about; (2) every claim/service-line loop in 277 (2200D/2200E/2220D/2220E) carries STC (Status Information) in addition to 276's own TRN/REF/AMT/DTP shape — STC is the segment that actually carries the claim status category/code/action/paid-amount answer, confirmed Mandatory with max>1 at all 6 of these loop positions.",
    "STC (new segment, see STC.json's own sourceRefs for its full element sourcing and the honest note that this schema models the full generic 12-position shape rather than a fully per-position-IG-verified subset, since the fetched HIPAA page's own STC usage table wasn't fully captured).",
    "All other segments (HL, NM1, TRN, REF, DTP, AMT, DMG, SVC) reused unchanged from the existing shared library — same reuse-safety confirmation as 276.json (no hardcoded fixedValue, sufficiently generic shape for this transaction's own needs)."
  ],
